From 27579162f45eecd9908e2c280edabb3f1b9dee1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite-Emulator Dev <dev@auralite-emu.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:05:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S4 update

STORE S4: AHCI breadth matrix.

Machine half (all measured against the guest's own contract):
- machine_t attach rows are per controller now ([AHCI_CTRLS][AHCI_MAX_ATTACH]);
  src/ahci.c runs one register instance per controller via
  ahci_register_ctrl(m, ctrl) -- controller 0 keeps the historical
  ahci_register() entry point and the exact [ahci] log spelling, controller 1
  logs as [ahci2].
- Second controller (--ahci2): PCI function 0:31:3 (8086:2922, class
  01/06/01) with ABAR2 at 0xFEB12000.  Placement is not arbitrary: the
  guest class scan is bus-0 dev/func ASCENDING (drivers/pci/pci.c
  pci_find_class_after, measured), so 31:3 binds after 0:31:2 and every
  S1-S3 'controller 0 at PCI 0:31.2' receipt keeps its numbering.  The
  guest maps 8 KiB per BAR5 (measured), hence 8 KiB window spacing.
- CLI: --ahci2, --sata2=img, --sata2-portN=img (an image on row 1 implies
  the controller).  --help now documents the storage family.

Tests: tests/test_ahci.c 15 -> 18 vectors (second-window independence and
per-controller GHC, port placement through the engine incl. TFES on a dark
port, cross-controller image isolation).  NEW
tests/integration/test_ahci_matrix.sh reproduces the QEMU
test_ahci_matrix.sh lanes A/B/C guest-side through the --keys-at=prompt
lane plus an unattached negative-control lane and a sequential determinism
pair.

Receipts (frozen kernel AuraLite-OS@0ed0d29 + initrd, measured):
- lane A: PASS: SATA read/write DMA works; typed write/cat round-trip
  laneaok on /fat; [fat32] PASS; zero FAIL/unsupported lines.
- lane B: hw port 1: SATA disk (sig=0x00000101); empty port 0 skipped;
  lanebok round-trip; determinism pair byte-identical.
- lane C: controller 0 at PCI 0:31.2 + controller 1 at PCI 0:31.3 +
  2 controller(s), 2 SATA device(s) ready; [ext2] blkdev 1 mounted at /ext2
  (2-disk boot); lanecok round-trip.
- lane E: 1 controller(s), 0 SATA device(s) ready + self-test: no devices.
make test + make test-sanitize green.
